main.c
--trace
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line 9 member: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line 10 fails: FAILURE$
^  s=\{ \.a=\{ -?\d+, -?\d+ \}, \.b=-?\d+ \}
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^warning: ignoring
^Invariant check failed
--
The declaration of a field-sensitive struct must only make the decision
procedure aware of the individual fields, which are what all other steps use.
Converting the struct as a whole made the incremental SMT back-end fail, as it
does not support the concatenation that the struct equality was flattened to.
The trace must still show the value of each field at the point of declaration.
